You noticed it, so you can do something about it. :-)

The "inventory" message is so apparent that you really shouldn't kick
the door down; that has little to do with carelessness, if you were a
good friend of mine I'd rather call it stupidity. :-)

Try changing your general strategy with doors! Don't kick them down,
they are invaluable as a tactical means to control movement of monsters
and pets; an intact door can save your life in many ways. Even closing
the doors is a good move if you to get known about intelligent monsters
approaching (you hear a door being openend from afar).

Intentionally hitting floating a floating eye is also no carelessness,
my friend, it's also stupidity. :-)

To avoid the floating eye thing you should get used to doing two things;
start using the advanced move commands (see Guidebook for all details)
to avoid running into one by accident, it pays, and to kill it always
use ranged weapons (daggers, darts, stones, ...).

